## 16. Audit Trail Fields — Universal Pattern

These fields are **system-captured** (never user-typed) on **every Create/Edit/Delete** operation across all master and transaction pages:

| Field | How Obtained | Source | Page Dependency |
|---|---|---|---|
| `IPAddress` | `Request.UserHostAddress` | HTTP request | None — auto from server |
| `MACAddress` | **DB Lookup** by IP | `SystemInfo.Where(IP == requestIP).Select(MACAddress)` | **🔗 System Info Master** — devices must be registered |
| `DeviceName` | **DB Lookup** by IP | `SystemInfo.Where(IP == requestIP).Select(DeviceName)` | **🔗 System Info Master** |
| `WindowsLoginUsername` | **DB Lookup** by IP | `SystemInfo.Where(IP == requestIP).Select(USERNAME)` | **🔗 System Info Master** |
| `Department` | **DB Lookup** by IP | `SystemInfo.Where(IP == requestIP).Select(DEPT)` | **🔗 System Info Master** |
| `CreatedDate` / `UpdatedDate` | `DateTime.Now` | Server clock | None |

> [!WARNING]
> If a workstation's IP is not registered in the System Info Master page, the audit trail fields (MAC, Device, User) will be **null**. Every workstation MUST be registered first.

